# VroomView — environment variable TEMPLATE (names only, NO real values).
#
# Setup:
#   1. Copy this file to .env.local:   cp .env.example .env.local
#   2. Fill in the values from your Supabase project's dashboard.
#   3. NEVER commit .env.local (it is git-ignored).
#
# Why these are safe to expose to the browser:
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_* variables are inlined into the client bundle by Next.js, so ONLY
#   public, non-secret values may use that prefix. The publishable (anon) key is
#   designed to be public — your data is protected by Supabase Row Level Security (RLS).
#   NEVER put a Supabase SECRET/service-role key in a NEXT_PUBLIC_ variable.

# Supabase project URL — Dashboard → Project Settings → Data API → Project URL
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=

# Supabase publishable (anon) key — Dashboard → Project Settings → API Keys
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
